{
  "$comment": "Language-neutral parity vectors for the Vogel Vault todo contract (shared/domain/src/todo.ts and android/domain/.../Todo.kt). The TypeScript and Kotlin suites both load this file so the two normalizers cannot drift. Semantics are pinned to convex/todoNormalize.ts + convex/dataFiles.ts (the emitter) and the legacy Swift compatibility DTO (the alias/ownership authority). When either of those changes, change this file in the same commit.",

  "$divergences": [
    "owner: Swift resolves owner ?? assignee; convex reads only `owner` and defaults to victor. The contract follows Swift, because owner is a visibility field and an assignee-only todo must land on the person it names.",
    "priority: convex does Number(priority || 0), which yields NaN for retained word priorities. The contract maps urgent/high=1, medium/normal=2, low=3 per Swift's decodePriority, then falls back to 0.",
    "dueDate: convex reads dueDate then due_date. The contract keeps that order and appends Swift's remaining chain (due, date, deadline, when) below it, then requires the result to be a real ISO calendar day — `when` is a Things bucket word, not a date.",
    "dueDate precedence: Swift prefers due_date over dueDate; convex prefers dueDate. They only differ when both are present AND disagree, which the emitter never produces because it writes both from one value. The contract follows convex.",
    "timestamps: convex uses new Date(str), which reads a zoneless datetime as LOCAL time. The contract parses strictly and treats a missing zone as UTC, so last-write-wins resolves identically on every device.",
    "flag/done: convex ORs the alias pairs (flag||flagged, done||completed) while Swift prefers the second of each. They differ only when the pair contradicts itself. The contract follows convex.",
    "status: `done` is set by status === \"completed\" exactly, case-sensitively, as convex does. Swift also accepts \"done\" and is case-insensitive."
  ],

